ing class’s formal passage.","short_summary":"The entering class begins its Hampden-Sydney journey by walking through the Bell Tower’s north opening.","evidence_claim":"Hampden-Sydney’s commencement traditions program states that freshmen entering in the fall pass through the Bell Tower’s north opening beneath “HUC VENITE IUVENES.”","source_url":"https://www.hsc.edu/Documents/Commencement/CommencProgram2017.pdf","source_title":"Hampden-Sydney College Commencement 2017 Program","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2017-05-14","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The ceremonial passage occurs during the entering-class program; access around the tower may be managed for the event.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hsc-class-year-bell-rings","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Class-Year Bell Rings","title":"Ring the Bell for Your Class Year","subtitle":"The entering class sounds the final two digits of its year","notes":"Listen for the class-year count during orientation and leave the rope to scheduled participants; the Class of 2025 rang it exactly 25 times.","short_summary":"A new class announces its arrival from Watkins Bell Tower with a year-specific number of rings.","evidence_claim":"At 2021 orientation, Class of 2025 students rang the Watkins Bell Tower bell 25 times to signify the beginning of their academic careers.","source_url":"https://www7.hsc.edu/news-index/new-tigers-2021","source_title":"New Tigers Roll In","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2021-08-26","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Bell access is controlled by the College; only designated participants should enter the tower or handle its rope.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hsc-hand-rung-class-bell","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Hand-Rung Clas